  "walkthroughs": [
    {
      "tag": "Stop 1",
      "h2": "Big control centre",
      "body_html": "<p class=\"big\">The <span class=\"hl p\">brain</span> weighs about <b>1.4 kg</b> and has billions of cells called <b>neurons</b>.</p><p>It runs everything — movement, thinking, breathing, feelings. 🧠</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Stop 2",
      "h2": "The lobes",
      "body_html": "<p>Each side of the brain has lobes:</p><ul><li><span class=\"hl p\">Frontal lobe</span> — planning, decisions, personality.</li><li><b>Parietal</b> — touch and space.</li><li><b>Temporal</b> — hearing and memory.</li><li><b>Occipital</b> — vision.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Stop 3",
      "h2": "Deeper regions",
      "body_html": "<p>Under the lobes:</p><ul><li><span class=\"hl y\">Cerebellum</span> — balance, riding a bike.</li><li><span class=\"hl y\">Amygdala</span> — fear, anger.</li><li><b>Hippocampus</b> — long-term memory.</li></ul><p>Together they keep you alive and you. ❤️</p>"
    }
  ],
